WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.180
Hey everyone, привет!

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:03.780
Welcome to привет, русский эпизод 31.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.900
Это 30 мая в 1926 года.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:07.900
I'm Olya,

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.720
and today we're going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:11.940
Ready, поехали.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.380
That means, let's go.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.500
Our word of the day is Dost, Dost.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:17.900
Let me say it slowly.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.760
Dost, the...

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:20.760
Now at normal speed.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.480
Dost, it means rain.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.640
Imagine the word Dost sounding like a gentle drip drop on the roof.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.900
D, Z makes it feel splashy and wet.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:30.920
Repeat after me.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:31.720
Say it slowly.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.000
Dost, D, D.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.860
Now say it at normal speed.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.540
Dost, D, great job.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:37.920
Let's try once more.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.620
Dost, D, you can use it in a simple sentence.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.360
Сегодня идёт дождь.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.640
Сегодня идёт дождь.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:44.580
It is raining today.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.920
Now let's build more weather words that go with our theme.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.560
The first one is Sonsa, Sonsa.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.340
It means sun.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.820
Sonsa starts like solar, both pointing to the bright star in the sky.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.720
Repeat after me, Sonsa.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:58.560
Sonsa.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:01.600
Next comes ветер, ветер, it means wind.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.560
ветер sounds like ветер, like an old wind that has blown for years.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.880
Repeat after me, ветер, ветер.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.220
Now we have Oblaco, Oblaco, it means cloud.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.620
Oblaco begins like Oblong, so picture a long fluffy shape in the sky.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.260
Repeat after me, Oblaco, Oblaco.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.060
Here is SNEC, SNEC, it means snow.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.660
SNEC rhymes with leg, and you can imagine snow covering your legs up to the knees.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:28.340
Repeat after me, SNEC, SNEC.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.120
Next is тепло, тепло, it means warm or warm.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.280
тепло sounds like tapet, but means nicely warm, not lukewarm.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.640
Repeat after me, тепло, тепло.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.840
Then we have холодно, холодно, it means cold.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.860
холодно begins like chili, both words describe when you need a jacket.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.500
Repeat after me, холодно, холодно.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.300
Now, гроза, гроза, it means thunderstorm.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.180
Grоза sounds like grows a big storm.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.080
Perfect for thunder and lightning.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.440
Repeat after me, гроза, гроза.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.700
Finally, радуга, радуга, it means rainbow.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:05.620
радуга sounds like rat plus uga, a happy arc of colors.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.820
Repeat after me, радуга, радуга.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.040
Now, let's look at one simple grammar pattern that ties these words together.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:16.240
We can say the weather with Shivodnya, followed by the weather word.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.000
Shivodnya means today, for example.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.400
Shivodnya тепло, it is warm today,

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.300
or Shivodnya холодно, it is cold today,

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.340
and Shivodnya идет дождь, it is raining today.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.240
In English, we often add ease and change the verb,

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.120
but in Russian, the weather word itself carries the meaning and stays simple.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.620
No extra verb is needed for temperature words.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.340
Now you can say the weather in Russian right away.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.960
Want to know a secret about one of today's words?

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.360
The Russian word солнце, and the English word solar,

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.100
are actually cousins from the same ancient roots.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.860
They both come from a very old word that simply meant sun.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.640
This word traveled through Latin as soul, giving us solar and sun,

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.740
while in Slavic languages, it became солнце.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.600
Along the way, it picked up a playful false friend.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.780
In some old texts, soul could hint at salt,

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.100
because the sun was seen as preserving life, like salt does.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.160
Be careful though, the real Russian word for salt is soul.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.920
Next time you see the word solar, or feel the sun on your face,

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.560
remember it is cousins with солнце.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.440
They both come from the same ancient word for the bright star above us.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.940
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.440
Russians love talking about the weather

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.020
because it changes dramatically across their huge country,

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:35.000
from snowy Siberia to sunny black sea beaches.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.580
A popular saying is,

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:42.420
there is no wet weather, only unsuitable clothing.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.820
It teaches that you can enjoy any weather if you dress right.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:47.620
Now it is practice time.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.060
For kids, draw a picture of today's weather

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.960
and label it with three new words,

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.020
солнце, дожд, облака.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.720
For adults, look out the window right now

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.380
and say out loud in Russian,

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.980
сегодня, followed by a weather word.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.200
Then add one more detail like,

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:04.500
сегодня идёт дожд,

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:06.860
молодец, that means well done.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.780
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.200
Practice saying today's words out loud, even just once,

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.260
and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:16.500
See you next time.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:18.340
Пока, that's Russian for Buy.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.560
This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.180
Editorial selection and analysis are my own.
